{{!
    @template theme_nit/core/welcome

    theme_nit override of core/welcome — intentionally renders NOTHING.

    Core (lib/classes/output/core_renderer::full_header) injects a one-time
    "Welcome, {firstname}! 👋" / "Hi, {firstname}! 👋" greeting into the page
    header on the user's home page (see \core_user::welcome_message() and the
    lang strings welcometosite / welcomeback). The EAAC front page is a branded
    marketing home built from our own section blocks, where that per-user
    greeting is off-design, so we suppress it site-wide by overriding the
    partial with an empty body. No core files are touched; the greeting's empty
    wrapper <div> in full_header collapses to zero height, so nothing shows.

    Blanking the lang strings would only empty the text and leave the box; this
    removes the whole section.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * welcomemessage - string (ignored here)
}}
